0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.01759128534786998,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":8.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4175127626844322,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":30.4,"_gate_incr_roic":0.10154209916413418,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":50.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.6872929794556901,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.4412515018056469,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.23283700415537023,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.001586620129348648,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.6,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05415162546925357,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":71.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.11851519691685719,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004042568912133348,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":93.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.00283,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"VICI Properties Inc. is a real estate investment trust that owns one of the largest portfolios of market-leading gaming, hospitality, wellness, entertainment and leisure destinations, including Caesars Palace Las Vegas, MGM Grand and the Venetian Resort Las Vegas. VICI Properties owns 103 experiential assets across a geographically diverse portfolio consisting of 63 gaming properties and 40 other experiential properties across the United States and Canada. The portfolio is comprised of approximately 130 million square feet and features approximately 66,000 hotel rooms and over 700 restaurants, bars, nightclubs and sports books. Its properties are occupied by industry-leading gaming, leisure and hospitality operators under long-term, triple-net lease agreements. VICI Properties has a growing array of real estate and financing partnerships with leading operators in other experiential sectors, including Cabot, Cain, Canyon Ranch, Chelsea Piers, Club Med, Great Wolf Resorts, Homefield, Kalahari Resorts and Lucky Strike Entertainment. VICI Properties also owns four championship golf courses and approximately 33 acres of undeveloped and underdeveloped land adjacent to the Las Vegas Strip. VICI Properties Inc. was established on July 05, 2016, and is based in New York, United States. VICI Properties Inc. was incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Edward Baltazar Pitoniak | CEO & Director | Age 69 | Compensation: $5.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 28 people. Revenue per employee of $143.1M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 47%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $89.6M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $578K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["VICI Properties Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $27.3B market cap on $4.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $2.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 63 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.90\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 69% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 40% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"VICI Properties Inc. $VICI Stock Purchased by Chicago Partners Investment Group LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/vici-properties-inc-vici-stock-purchased-by-chicago-partners-investment-group-llc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793955680.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.906,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"35,317 VICI Properties Inc. $VICI Shares Bought by International Assets Investment Management LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/35317-vici-properties-inc-vici-shares-bought-by-international-assets-investment-management-llc.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793871845.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.926,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Revenue Rises While Profit Falls Could Be A Game Changer For VICI Properties (VICI)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-vici/vici-properties/news/revenue-rises-while-profit-falls-could-be-a-game-changer-for","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793863967.362,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.013,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Did VICI Properties (NYSE:VICI) Lift Its Yearly Guidance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/why-did-vici-properties-nysevici-lift-its-yearly-guidance","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793819520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"How to Convert an $840,000 401(k) to a Roth IRA and Collect $4,050 a Month Tax-Free for Life","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/convert-840-000-401-k-184722000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793991338.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.178,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"If I Could Put $10,000